  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4 Dental Implants\n\nFixed Teeth vs. Removable\n\nCost & Compare\n\nDental Implant FAQ\n\nAesthetics\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nDental Crowns & Bridges\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nTreatments\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nOral Surgery\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nWho We Are\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nMeet Dr. Esam Nahlah\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nPatient Stories\n\nFor Doctors\n\nReferral Form\n\nContact Us\n\nBlog\n\nCurrent Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria: (703) 940-5410\n\nNew Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (571) 619-9442\n\nAlexandria: (571) 410-3430\n\nBook now\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n# Dental Implants in McLean, VA\n\n\n\n## The Lasting Solution for a Single Missing Tooth\n\n\n“I Haven’t Stopped Smiling Since I Got My Dental Implants!” – Yolanda\n\nSchedule Now\n\n\n## Patient Story\n\n\nEliminate The Risk Of Human Error With 3D Guided Dental Implant Placement\n\n\n## Long-Lasting, Life-Changing Dental Implants\n\n\nAre you self-conscious about the current state of your oral health and esthetics? Are you missing some or all of your teeth? Are you experiencing pain or discomfort with your dentures? If so, permanent dental implants can offer incredible, life-changing results and can restore your quality of life with a brilliant, perfect new smile. Dental implants offer the same look and functionality of natural teeth, so you can brush and floss like normal, plus eat all of the foods you love with little to no pain or discomfort! Unlike dentures, dental implants are a permanent solution to missing teeth. Give our office a call today and speak with Dr. Esam Nahlah and his professional dental team about your dental implant candidacy.\n\n\n### Find out if you're a\n\n\n\n## candidate for dental implants\n\n\n\n#### Answer the Following Questions To Learn more about our pricing and financing options.\n\n\n\n## Dental Implants: The Gold Standard for Missing Teeth\n\n\nUnlike traditional dentures, dental implants are permanently anchored to the jawbone, meaning no slipping over time and no painful friction as a result of rubbing on the gums while eating and speaking. Implants consist of three main parts: a titanium post that is surgically placed into the jaw, an abutment which acts as an anchor for the replacement tooth, and finally, the customized replacement tooth (prosthetic) itself. At Dental Group of Tysons in McLean, VA, we offer free second opinions on dental implant surgery, as well as five-year warranties on all of our implant procedures (warranties mandate pre-care general cleanings every six months).\n\nView More Results\n\n\n## Personalized Attention, Customized Results\n\n\nDepending on your unique situation, several different dental implant options can help you achieve a perfect smile and a set of stunning, brilliantly white new teeth. Single dental implants are often the best option for a single tooth that has been damaged due to physical impact. Implant supported dentures, full mouth dental implants and implant-supported bridges are practical options that can replace several (or all) of your missing teeth. Full-mouth dental implants are the gold standard for replacing missing teeth, while implant-supported bridges and dentures offer an intermediate option in terms of both price and functionality. Depending on your personal situation and the current state of your oral health, Dr. Nahlah will determine the perfect implant option for you in terms of helping to craft a stunning smile and giving you back the quality of life you deserve.\n\nSingle Implants\n\nImplant Supported Bridge\n\nImplant Supported Dentures\n\nFull Mouth Dental Implants\n\nDr. Nahlah Discusses Single Dental Implants\n\n\n## How the Dental Implant Process Works\n\n\nThe first step of any dental implant process is to schedule an appointment with Dr. Nahlah for an initial consultation. The surgical process itself is carried out in a single visit, followed by an approximately four-month healing process (during which the implant posts will permanently fuse with the jawbone). After your surgery, you will come in for two separate appointments: a routine checkup followed by a final visit. In this final visit, Dr. Nahlah will place your permanent set of new teeth! Dr. Nahlah uses state-of-the-art zirconia fixed bridges for full mouth implant surgery, which represents the pinnacle of oral health restoration. Our team also offers a variety of sedation options, ensuring your dental implant surgery will be as smooth and pain-free as possible. Find out today if you are a candidate for world-class dental implants.\n\n\n## Fixed Implants vs. Traditional Dentures\n\n\nFixed dental implants are quickly becoming the gold standard for missing teeth replacement. While dentures are prone to slipping and movement over time, implants are permanently fused with the jawbone, meaning little to no possibility of movement, even after years of use. Implants also support the jaw and facial bones, and due to the fusing of the titanium implant post, actually limit jawbone recession! Also, although the initial cost of dental implants is higher than that of dentures, implants typically require less maintenance and repair, meaning lower cost over the long-term. No matter your personal situation, an investment into dental implants is a long-term investment into your health, happiness and overall quality of life.\n\nReplacing A Missing Or Cracked Front Tooth\n\n\n## Advantages Of Dental Implants vs. Dentures\n\n\nImplants permanently replace one or more missing teeth with new dental prosthetics\n\nImplant prosthetics look, feel and function just like normal teeth\n\nImplants return over 99% of the durability and functionality of natural teeth\n\nImplants limit jawbone recession and support facial bone structure\n\nEasier maintenance and hygiene, less pain, and less need for repair and maintenance\n\n\n## Top 5 Mistakes People Make with Dental Implants\n\n\nDo you have all the information you need to make the right decisions about dental implants? Don’t make any of these five common mistakes. Our exclusive checklist will steer you in the right direction.\n\n\n## Affordable and Accessible Dental Implant Options\n\n\nAt Dental Group of Tysons, our team believes that every patient – no matter their financial situation – should be afforded the opportunity to receive dental implants that restore health, happiness and functionality to daily life. We gladly accept most major dental insurance providers, and we offer a variety of affordable, third-party financing options that allow patients to make convenient monthly payments on their implant procedure. If you’re in need of replacement teeth, speak with us today about affordable payment options. No matter your financial situation, don’t let anything get in the way of achieving a perfect smile that restores your confidence and reinstates a healthy, happy lifestyle. Call our office today and start the journey to complete oral restoration.\n\n\n## Our Patients tell the story best\n\n\nPlay\n\n\n## Experience the Life-Changing Benefits of Dental Implants\n\n\nCall today and schedule your dental implant consultation in McLean, VA with Dental Group of Tysons.\n\nBook Now\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddresses:\n\nTysons Corner\n\n7901 Jones Branch Dr., Suite 220\n\nMcLean, VA 22102\n\nNew Patients: (571) 619-9442\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria\n\n2855 Duke St,\n\nAlexandria, VA 22314\n\nNew Patients: (571) 410-3430\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 940-5410\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 8:00am – 2:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-On-4® Implants\n\nCrowns & Bridges\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nMeet the Doctor\n\nAbout Us\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\n2025 Dr. Nahlah. All rights reserved",
